      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Kvasir era un ser muy sabio. Los dioses lo habían hecho de su saliva, para sellar una paz.",
          "en": "Kvasir was a very wise being. The gods had made him from their spit, to seal a peace."
        },
        {
          "es": "Podía responder cualquier pregunta, y recorría el mundo enseñando a la gente.",
          "en": "He could answer any question, and he walked the world teaching people."
        },
        {
          "es": "Un día dos enanos, Fjalar y Galar, lo llevaron aparte y lo mataron.",
          "en": "One day two dwarves, Fjalar and Galar, took him aside and killed him."
        },
        {
          "es": "Dejaron correr su sangre en dos cubas y un caldero, y la mezclaron con miel.",
          "en": "They let his blood run into two vats and a kettle. They mixed it with honey."
        },
        {
          "es": "Así nació un hidromiel mágico, una bebida de miel. Quien lo bebía se volvía poeta y sabio.",
          "en": "The result was a magic mead, a honey drink. Whoever drank it became a poet and a sage."
        }
      ],
